      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5e4bc438d0966f5979b9a456",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 20
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Regardless of what the exact action is, some kind of decision needs to be made regarding mods. The issue is that a significant number of highly desired features that are absent from the game are driving people towards mods, and in ever greater numbers. It's creating a culture creep of widely discussed, shared and normalised modification. Whilst most of those mods might be perfectly benign, non-invasive and non-malicious, there are others that exist which do push the boundaries of what powers players should have, or otherwise are outright malicious. The culture around this is also a neighbour to modded-client use, and brings people closer to that highly undesirable side of the community. The more malicious client/mod use that exists, the more people who will be attracted/compelled to seek out their own clients for sake of protecting themselves and having a means to combat it, for lack of any other viable alternative. This in turn only escalates the entire situation, and turns things into some kind of ridiculous hacker arms race.\nThis problem really can't be understated. I've been under the impression that the current impending update from the VRC team is hopefully bringing some major reworks to networking and security, but regardless of if it is or isn't, it really needs to be a top priority for getting fixed ASAP.\nFix security. Fix the feature gap.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
