      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Pretty sure if VRC added a client scan so that every client must match their copy 1:1 in name and file size after each major update, there'd be a nice ban wave. Whether malicious or not. Plenty of games already do this. \nPretty sure it's been the case that something similar has happened before. Just a heads up. The ban wave would continue until the mod makers patched their own mods or made them a third-party executable. ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯\nBut yes, official support somewhere down the line would be nice. I've been running vanilla in VRC for over 2 years without issue though. Impatience or entitlement are perfectly fine being punishable as things stand currently.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
