      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "most of the people I knew who were using mods were doing it for very specific reasons- finding people in huge maps (which if map makers would adopt the teleport menu from booth that would be far less of an issue) and having more avatar favorites (which vrc still just does not have anywhere near enough, and there's a lot of excellent or hilarious public models out there that don't have a corresponding avatar pedastal in a world somewhere).  Give people a better number of avatar favorites, and publicly encourage better teleport options in huge maps, and I'm willing to bet the majority of mod users would stop having a real use for them.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
